Hello,

I use the following instructions to save data into a remote file.

> csvFileName <- 'stat.csv'
> write.table( x = statData , file = csvFileName , append = TRUE , sep = "," , col.names = NA , qmethod = "double" )

It works locally well (i.e. with runApp()) At the first session, the file is created and the session data are stored. The next session, the session data are appended. But on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> it doesn't work ? The file creation and update don't work : after several sessions when I download the bundle nothing new appears.

In the same way, the following instruction works locally well but doesn't work on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> where I've got an access denied error.
> ftpUpload( what = csvFileName , to = uploadURL , userpwd = 'userId:userPwd' ) # uploadURL is the url where to upload

Does someone know how to fix it ?
Thank you in advance,
Stéfane

